{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/694618-learning-unfavored-gifts","id":694618,"title":"Learning Unfavored Gifts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-09T00:38:51-07:00","id":694618,"title":"Learning Unfavored Gifts","content":"How difficult is it most likely storwise to learn an unfavored gift?<br /> <br /> I know it probaly depends a lot <br /> <br /> is it probaly safe to say that Sense Wyrm, or Lunas Armor are probaly VERY easy to talk a spirit into teaching, as their favored for so many groups.<br /> <br /> I can easily see a quest occuring because you WANT a gift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T01:39:48-07:00","id":694683,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem is that the books don't really have a solid in-game explanation for what &quot;causes&quot; favoring in Gifts to occur. I've been in games where the ST had no story difference between favored and not; story difficulty was based solely on the Rank of the Gift and how the spirit in question felt about the Garou in question. The difference in XP cost was considered an extra &quot;tax&quot; on the process Garou go through to learn Gifts rather than anything about what spirits might think about an Ahroun Glasswalker trying to learn Spirit Speech. I've also been in games where the ST increase the story cost of Gifts under the assumption that Gaian aligned spirits enforced the favored/not thing as a real part of spirit politics.<br /> <br /> Both extremes work, and don't really contrast with the setting material. Though it lends very different tones to play (and the first option sees a lot more cherry picking of specific Gifts; which is why I think so many STs favor the second).<br /> <br /> So, what I think is the best approach is to discuss the hows and whys as a group to decide what the in-game explanation of this is, and from there it should be more clear how to proceed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T05:10:37-07:00","id":694742,"title":"","content":"This is how we have done it in the past. As Heavy Arms has stated, each game can be a little different and the storyteller has a lot of play in this area.<br /> <br /> If your character doesn't know someone with that gift or have seen the gift being used during the course of the game, I feel the most important part of this is explaining how a Garou knows that a gift exists. Some tribes are very stingy with knowledge of their gifts (Silver Fang/Shadowlord) while others are willing to share in order to strengthen ties (Bone Gnawer/Children of Gaia). All gifts are not common knowledge. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I don't know if the W20 books says this but in one of the older books it said that Garou learning gifts outside their Auspice was often frowned upon by Elders because the Garou was trying to be something that he isn't. Other then Tribal/Sept politics I don't think this is often hard to overcome as long as its not the common occurrence. When going up in rank the first gift bought from the new rank should always be from the Garou's Auspice, again because of tradition.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Learning a Gift from another tribe usually requires the Garou to be on good terms with at least one member of the tribe (generally a packmate) who can summon the appropriate spirit. Even then, the Garou must convince the spirit she is worthy of its blessings, and that she won't turn them against its tribal allies.<br /> <br /> Breed gifts are probably the most ambiguous in this regards, they seem to be based around the nature of the Garou in question. I think its simply this nature that makes them unfavorable. I think a Homid who has a &quot;back to nature mentality&quot; would be more likely to pick up Lupus gifts then one who spent his entire life in a skyscraper. I normally don't impose many road blocks.</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T09:31:44-07:00","id":695016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/694618-learning-unfavored-gifts?p=694742#post694742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if the W20 books says this but in one of the older books it said that Garou learning gifts outside their Auspice was often frowned upon by Elders because the Garou was trying to be something that he isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is at least maintained with the idea that acting outside your Auspice is a Renown hit. So a Garou that's picking up a lot of out-of-splat Gifts might find themselves racking up Renown hits, that the Elders then pick up on and frown upon.<br /> <br /> It's actually not a bad &quot;mid-ground&quot; between the two extremes I listed. Letting players pick between a story cost of increased effort to get the spirit to teach, and agree it makes sense for the Garou to learn the Gift (ex: A Ragabash might try to convince a spirit that they need Spirit Speech to spy on a nest of banes and understand what they're saying; so they're learning it for the duties of their Auspice, not to step on the toes of the Theurges), or skip the extra learning steps but take a Renown hit as the spirits assume you're acting out of Auspice, and the social consequences of doing so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Learning a Gift from another tribe usually requires the Garou to be on good terms with at least one member of the tribe (generally a packmate) who can summon the appropriate spirit. Even then, the Garou must convince the spirit she is worthy of its blessings, and that she won't turn them against its tribal allies. </div> </div> </div>This one is always going to be a bit problematic for me, because the spirits that are listed as teaching Gifts have no direct correlation to the splats in question. A Gift being taught by a member of Owl's brood doesn't ensure that it's a Silent Strider Gift, nor does a Gift being favored by the Striders ensure it is taught by part of Owl's brood.<br /> <br /> If my Garou is an Uktena with Roadrunner as their pack Totem... what does being friendly with the Silent Striders matter to being able to learn Speed of Thought?<br /> <br /> Issues like this are one of the reasons I tend to want to get a group playing WtA long term to pin down a specific explanation for the in-game reasoning here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T10:02:31-07:00","id":695052,"title":"","content":"I would actually allow the Uktena to learn the gift in that case. Having Roadrunner as a totem is just as good if not better then having a Silent Strider to speak on your behalf and obviously you don't need him to summon the spirit. More-so in that scenario because I don't believe that Roadrunner is a member of Owl's Brood. I am more strict on gifts that are taught by Brood specific spirits and tribal Ancestor spirits then I am on gifts that are taught by unaffiliated spirits.<br /> <br /> My greatest concern is, how did that Garou know that the gift exists in the first place? and then, how did he know what kind of spirit teaches that gift? Simply selecting a gift based on the fact it exists in the book doesn't work for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","user":"Derzhuzad","date":". 10-09-2015, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T10:19:23-07:00","id":695092,"title":"","content":"Oh!? I think most will understand almost ANY garou wanting Sense Wyrm, to be aware of problems, or Mothers Touch, to stabilize a fallen comrade... but a Theruge wanting Razor Claws or Silver Claws, will probaly raise... questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T10:50:06-07:00","id":695108,"title":"","content":"Sense wyrm is probably the easiest gift to justify and the easiest to obtain because literally every spirit can teach it. Mother's Touch is not the same. it is taught be Bear and Unicorn spirits. Unicorn Spirits being part of Unicorns brood means they are out and Bear is known for being stingy with his Gifts. Bear remembers what gifts the Gurahl shared with the Garou and he knows how the Garou turned around and used them against the Gurahl. I would have him be very wary of teaching anyone but a Theurage this gift.<br /> <br /> Likewise, its a Theurage's job to act as support and an Ahroun's job to fight. If the Ahroun is healing then who is fighting? I would have any Ahroun learning this gift catch a little crap from his Ahroun peers and elders. Yes, it can be justified but its one of those gifts where I think it catches attention in this scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T23:53:14-07:00","id":695806,"title":"","content":"Favored gifts are part of the Pact with the appropriate spirit brood. Every Garou is inheriting a lot of earlier work done to make the Tribal, Auspice, and Breed spirits favor you. It's like asking family members for help. Those spirits either know you, or know your family. <br /> <br /> Going to other spirits is like asking that guy down the street who doesn't know you. Whether he does or not depends on the specific person, what mood he's in when you ask, and the reasonableness of the request. Usually it is best to already be doing things that cause those spirits to become familiar with you and develop a favorable opinion.<br /> <br /> I am more inclined to allow out of bounds Gifts be taught if its appropriate the pack Totem or its brood can do so. If you are a Fianna and belong to a pack with Owl as its totem, then I'd be more willing for that Fianna to learn some Silent Strider Gifts than I would for Wendigo Gifts. Of course, Bone Gnawer Tribal Gifts may be less likely since those spirits may not like Owl. Of course, this is not entirely perfect for the reasons Heavy Arms laid out (Tribal Gifts and appropriate spirits who teach them sometimes seem to have little logic in terms of spirits and the actual Spirit Brood of the Tribal totem). The Garou though should be in good stead with their pack totem, and if there are particularly &quot;signature&quot; Tribal Gifts, they are more likely not to be taught. Ubqiuitous Gifts found in many places are more prone to be taught if asked.<br /> <br /> Auspice Gifts are less likely to be taught since that is not so much based on a Tribal totem spirit brood, but the favor of Luna. If the Garou in question is particularly exemplar in their auspice, then it is much easier for spirits to teach them the odd Gift belonging to another auspice as it won't interfere with their duties. If the Garou isn't doing their auspice roll well, then the spirits are less likely to teach them less it encourages them to continue to stray.<br /> <br /> The higher rank of the Garou, the more likely spirits will teach them out of bounds Gifts. Cliaths never learn out of bounds gifts. Starting at Fostern, their pack totem may being considering to aid them in learning Gifts associated with their brood. At Adren and above, out of scope breed or auspice Gifts become possible.<br /> <br /> In the games I run, I just don't let players just spend XP and get the Gifts. They have to roleplay it out because I want to encourage spirits being part of the world, and to emphasize these are <i>gifts</i>, not something to be taken for granted. Usually I won't require too hard a standard. If they ever ask for something out of bounds, they better really sell it to me, otherwise the spirit will just say no.<br /> <br /> One thing I avoid is the idea that spirits should feel compelled to teach certain Gifts because the Garou in question &quot;need&quot; them or &quot;should&quot; have them. Spirits don't care about that. They've been around a very long time, and seen a lot of Garou come and go and seen Wyrm threats come and go. Spirits are not the supplicants, the individual Garou in question always are. No Spirit should ever think &quot;I need to give these Garou Sense Wyrm or Spirit Speech because what they'll do with it should be of benefit to me in some way.&quot; Garou always need to earn the Spirit's favor, any presumptions on the Garou's part is not giving the spirits their proper respect. Spirits do not act like humans or Garou and live in their world. They have their own natures, agendas, realities, and values. Proper Chiminage is always needed, and must be paid in advance - no spirit performs a favor on &quot;credit&quot; or future promise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T01:58:59-07:00","id":695854,"title":"","content":"Lots of good advice in this thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/694618-learning-unfavored-gifts?p=695806#post695806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I avoid is the idea that spirits should feel compelled to teach certain Gifts because the Garou in question &quot;need&quot; them or &quot;should&quot; have them. Spirits don't care about that. They've been around a very long time, and seen a lot of Garou come and go and seen Wyrm threats come and go. Spirits are not the supplicants, the individual Garou in question always are. No Spirit should ever think &quot;I need to give these Garou Sense Wyrm or Spirit Speech because what they'll do with it should be of benefit to me in some way.&quot; Garou always need to earn the Spirit's favor, any presumptions on the Garou's part is not giving the spirits their proper respect. Spirits do not act like humans or Garou and live in their world. They have their own natures, agendas, realities, and values. Proper Chiminage is always needed, and must be paid in advance - no spirit performs a favor on &quot;credit&quot; or future promise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, for the most part, but there is an exception that proves the rule: I have had spirits bestow gifts prior to receiving chiminage, only to demand favors or actions from the Garou later. Usually these spirits are not Gaian: ghosts, Weaver-slaves, dream-entities or other stranger things are all capable of sharing some of their secrets to the Garou (the rank 3 'Ghost Touched' Silent Strider gift is one example). Of course, since these beings don't hold to the same old pacts the totems do, such deals are often fraught with risks.<br /> <br /> I tend to be a bit of a hardass when it comes to allowing out of tribe gifts to be learned- I don't use tribal weaknesses and I feel like the mechanical differentiation of the gifts helps give a more concrete feel to the tribes. But I do very similar things to what others here have suggested- getting in good with a particular totem's brood will open up access to gifts that would otherwise be off-limits. Roleplaying out such things lets you impress on the players what a big deal gifts are, and it gives them a sense of achievement when they successfully engender the respect of an out-of-tribe totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T02:16:50-07:00","id":695864,"title":"","content":"This is very much a question of what your storyeller feels is right. The concept behind favoured gifts is that certain spirits are closer to you and therefore make it easier for you to learn them. While you can learn most &quot;foreign&quot; gifts up to level 3, beyond that is usually quite a big beef to get the biggest secrets of the Fera groups.<br /> <br /> I usually make it more of a story to learn gifts. Everyone needs to find, persuade and study under a spirit to get a Gift. It makes for fun stories. The key difference is that the favoured spirits will be more inclined to help you and treat you better once you get to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T10:01:55-07:00","id":696221,"title":"","content":"Can you learn a gift from another garou, for example a pack mate or sept elder? I was under the impression that you can. So for example my ragabash could ask my packmate theurge to teach me spirit speach so that i can eavesdrop on a couple of banes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T10:25:58-07:00","id":696235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/694618-learning-unfavored-gifts?p=696221#post696221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you learn a gift from another garou, for example a pack mate or sept elder? I was under the impression that you can. So for example my ragabash could ask my packmate theurge to teach me spirit speach so that i can eavesdrop on a couple of banes.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can but it takes a lot longer. In game times its the difference of a few hours versus a month of practice time. Again, its something that Elders frown upon doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T10:37:46-07:00","id":696243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/694618-learning-unfavored-gifts?p=696235#post696235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can but it takes a lot longer. In game times its the difference of a few hours versus a month of practice time. Again, its something that Elders frown upon doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have any references on that? The Book of Auspices takes quite a bit of page count to demonstrate how Auspices can be quite broad, and how there can be quite a bit of overlap between them, justifying all sorts of exotic gift combinations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T11:12:33-07:00","id":696266,"title":"","content":"Which part are you looking for reference on? I was paraphrasing pg 152 of the W20 int he part you quoted.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">Werewolves are also capable of teaching Gifts to one <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">another, but this process is neither fast nor easy. Learning <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">a Gift from another Garou is a long process of trial and <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">error, of attempting to achieve communion with another <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">werewolf and emulate the shape of his soul. At best, the <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">process takes a full lunar month. Most elders strongly discourage this practice, viewing it as unacceptably risky on <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">a number of levels. Wielding incomplete mastery of Gifts <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">such as Silver Claws, for example, can be not only painful, <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">but dangerous to the Garou and to others in his pack or <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">sept. Moreover, the level and depth of sustained intimacy <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">necessary for werewolves to teach Gifts to one another can <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">strain the bounds of the Litany, and more than a few metis <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">have resulted from tutoring sessions gone too far.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T11:22:54-07:00","id":696299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/694618-learning-unfavored-gifts?p=696235#post696235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can but it takes a lot longer. In game times its the difference of a few hours versus a month of practice time. Again, its something that Elders frown upon doing.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/694618-learning-unfavored-gifts?p=696243#post696243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you have any references on that? The Book of Auspices takes quite a bit of page count to demonstrate how Auspices can be quite broad, and how there can be quite a bit of overlap between them, justifying all sorts of exotic gift combinations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember reading this as well (but I don't remember the thing about the elders frowning on taking the month-long route to learning a Gift), but I can't recall the exact reference. I'm pretty sure it would have to be in one of the corebooks, probably the Revised corebook and I would expect a reference to it in W20 as well. Stay tuned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T12:17:42-07:00","id":696379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/694618-learning-unfavored-gifts?p=696266#post696266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which part are you looking for reference on? I was paraphrasing pg 152 of the W20 int he part you quoted.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">Werewolves are also capable of teaching Gifts to one <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">another, but this process is neither fast nor easy. Learning <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">a Gift from another Garou is a long process of trial and <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">error, of attempting to achieve communion with another <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">werewolf and emulate the shape of his soul. At best, the <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">process takes a full lunar month. Most elders strongly discourage this practice, viewing it as unacceptably risky on <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">a number of levels. Wielding incomplete mastery of Gifts <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">such as Silver Claws, for example, can be not only painful, <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">but dangerous to the Garou and to others in his pack or <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">sept. Moreover, the level and depth of sustained intimacy <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">necessary for werewolves to teach Gifts to one another can <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">strain the bounds of the Litany, and more than a few metis <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">have resulted from tutoring sessions gone too far.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the quote, the thing about Garou teaching Garou not being ideal has always been there. And while it's looked at suspiciously, it isn't a shooting offense. I find the whole concept of fraternisation leading to Litany breaches kinda excessive, though.<br /> <br /> What I was curious about is where does the information about Elders not liking Garou diversifying their Gifts come from. I was kinda distracted when posting and just latched onto your last line, since that was a sentiment repeated through and through the thread, so I'd love to hear more, as it pretty much contradicts the Book of Auspices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T13:25:42-07:00","id":696456,"title":"","content":"Ok, so the thing about elders disfavoring the month-long route to learning Gifts is because it's dangerous, not because of an unreasonable bias like I at first thought. That makes sense. And this sort of companionship between teacher and student has led to more than a few metis being conceived? Wow, that's something I hadn't considered. It makes sense after a fashion, though.<br /> <br /> It's probably an unconscious bias on my part, but whenever I envision a mentor-student relationship, it's always an older man teaching a younger male student so the romantic element doesn't enter into my thinking at all. But (with some tribal and/or sept) exceptions, the Garou females fight alongside their male brethren as equals, so it's entirely possible for a mentor-student relationship to be male-female or female-male. (Homosexual liasons among Garou teacher-student relationships may or may not exist, but they don't lead to metis being conceived, so I'll leave that alone.) So it's entirely possible for romantic feelings to crop up in that situation. In light of that, I have to disagree with Asmodai about Litany breaches in this sort of situation being excessive, as he called it. Considering that Garou best relate to other Garou before they can relate to humans or wolves, it makes sense that romantic feelings might crop up in a Garou mentor-student relationship. Just another facet of the tragic nature of the Garou, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T18:22:03-07:00","id":696680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/694618-learning-unfavored-gifts?p=695052#post695052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My greatest concern is, how did that Garou know that the gift exists in the first place? and then, how did he know what kind of spirit teaches that gift? Simply selecting a gift based on the fact it exists in the book doesn't work for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Spirits are in constant need of an ego boost, especially the ones who help out, particularly if it is regular. Galliards probably tell the stories about how a Garou demographic won the assistance of a spirit house more than any other set of stories, simply because the spirits would be offended from anything less.<br /> <br /> Even the out of Tribe Gifts are probably explained in stories where they are used as prayers of thanks offered to each spirit whose Gifts were used by the hero of the story after the legend is told.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 10-11-2015, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T18:29:00-07:00","id":696683,"title":"","content":"Why do Skindancers need to spend more for gifts in general then Normal garou for an unfavored Gift?<br /> <br /> is it just the Skindancers have trouble finding a spirit corrupt enough to teach them many gifts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T18:34:34-07:00","id":696685,"title":"","content":"Maybe their spirits lack a certain strength, a certain attachment to the spirit world without a Tribal Totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T18:36:13-07:00","id":696687,"title":"","content":"The Renown part of their spirits may also play a role in that as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T19:38:30-07:00","id":696742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/694618-learning-unfavored-gifts?p=696680#post696680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Spirits are in constant need of an ego boost, especially the ones who help out, particularly if it is regular. Galliards probably tell the stories about how a Garou demographic won the assistance of a spirit house more than any other set of stories, simply because the spirits would be offended from anything less.<br /> <br /> Even the out of Tribe Gifts are probably explained in stories where they are used as prayers of thanks are offered to each spirit whose Gifts were used by the hero of the story after the legend is told.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sometimes you could say he shot beams of light from his eyes or thunder from his arse and that sure sounds like it MIGHT be a gift. It could also be a euphemism or someone just telling a story. Someone may be telling his interpretation of what actually happened during that event. If the character hasn't taken the time to do some research in character about certain tricks then that is not really justification for knowing a gift is real. Could they use that as a basis for trying to actually get there hands on that gift? Yes, but that isn't the end of it, there is still some roleplay to be had. Otherwise players forget that each one is a gift that shouldn't be taken for granted. This is just my opinion and others surely do it differently, don't think either way is wrong as long as the story supports it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/694618-learning-unfavored-gifts?p=696683#post696683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do Skindancers need to spend more for gifts in general then Normal garou for an unfavored Gift?<br /> is it just the Skindancers have trouble finding a spirit corrupt enough to teach them many gifts?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my 2 cents, I have seen storytellers handle them differently so take this how ever you like. Skin Dancers actually get a cost break if you think about it, Rank x6. They are effectively Ronin who have banded together into a group so why don't they pay Rank x7? I think this is because as they have mentioned in the learning gifts section on page 514 of the W20, they have started to make spirit allies that Ronin normally don't have access to. Now, if a skin dancer takes Minotaur as their totem then they get even more of a break, i say this because his write up specifically says that they learn gift through him at 'out-of-tribe' cost, so his follower get the Rank x5 break on their gifts as part of his boon.<br /> <br /> Not all Skin Dancers like or are even willing to deal with Banes. They are all tainted yes, but some factions aren't willing to go any further down that rabbit hole. Some are actually trying to find other spirit allies that aren't trying to lead them into the Wyrm's ranks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T19:42:33-07:00","id":696743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/694618-learning-unfavored-gifts?p=696379#post696379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the quote, the thing about Garou teaching Garou not being ideal has always been there. And while it's looked at suspiciously, it isn't a shooting offense. I find the whole concept of fraternisation leading to Litany breaches kinda excessive, though.<br /> <br /> What I was curious about is where does the information about Elders not liking Garou diversifying their Gifts come from. I was kinda distracted when posting and just latched onto your last line, since that was a sentiment repeated through and through the thread, so I'd love to hear more, as it pretty much contradicts the Book of Auspices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honest truth, I did some digging today and I can't find it. I can't remember where I got that from and if my memory serves me right it was from something older then Book of Auspices. This ideology may very well have changed and I missed it because I haven't given that book a thorough reading and only ever used it for the gifts it had inside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T12:43:18-08:00","id":754784,"title":"","content":"oh 2 more gift cases?<br /> <br /> Lunas blessing... cant see a garou Who would NOT want it.... badly<br /> <br /> on out of tribe gifts... is it safe to say that anyone who would NEVER be accepted into the tribe (namely (Males for black furys, and homid for red talons) Will probaly have a hard time learning a tribal gift, to say the least... unless a personal friend decides to quietly teach it to them.<br /> <br /> Woe to him or her, if their elders find out and disapprove...<br /> <br /> Curse of Lycaon Though... I think... in spite of its high level, is a gift Red talons would be willing enough to teach to any elder wishing to learn it..<br /> <br /> As when a request to learn another tribes gifts is made &quot;What could this be used for if turned against us?&quot; Is what will be asked...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T03:54:26-08:00","id":756207,"title":"","content":"The legend about the first gift (in one of the anthologies iirc, Drums around the fire maybe), states that if you see a spirit do something (or possibly only suspect it is able to do something) you can petition to get that power taught...<br /> <br /> So, being instructed by a member of a given tribe doesn't seem necessary to lean a gift. Keeping secret what spirit teaches a certain gift certainly seems to be a way to protect tribal gifts, but a skilled theurge or pretty much anyone who is as creative as the author who designed the gift for the rulebook can come up with a spirit that logically should be able to bestow the feat to the character - so keeping something secret pretty much everyone could figure out on his own ain't that effective.<br /> <br /> Whether or not spirits enforce the tribal tie regarding their gifts is unknown. It might be the case if a gift is taught by a vassal of the tribal totem, but for more independent spirits it might be possible, that the gifts are taught regardless.<br /> <br /> Finally, it could be the case that spirits find it to exhausting to bestow gifts to people you don't have a natural knack for them and therefore need the extra convincing. If the rules regarding the instruction ability are applied to gifts, the spirit also would need to invest more time. But since the time to teach gifts is a lot less than other teaching the rules should not be used without conversion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T05:44:59-08:00","id":756335,"title":"","content":"think I was right about the &quot;How could this be used against us&quot; bit.<br /> <br /> Oh another question?<br /> <br /> ideas how elders will feel on learning gifts from other Breeds?<br /> <br /> a question just occured to me, if A lupus or metis uses Bury the wolf they are also locked in homid form?<br /> <br /> I think in a lot of cases it would be allowed maybe not encouraged but rarely discouraged either... <br /> <br /> As in pre modern times their were few Metis out there to learn Metis Gifts someone has to have Totem gift<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 11-05-2015, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}